        {
            "name": "Output Cache (manual perf)",
            "description": "Verify output caching + tag eviction by hand. Login (Admin) first.\n1) Run 'GET Subjects (1st — cache miss)' then 'GET Subjects (2nd — cache HIT)': the 2nd should be noticeably faster (served from cache, no DB hit) — each request logs its responseTime to the Postman console.\n2) Run 'Create Subject (evicts cache)', then 'GET Subjects (after evict — fresh)': the list reflects the new subject immediately (the write evicted the 'subjects' tag).\nNote: responses also vary by Accept-Language and (for teacher/student endpoints) by the signed-in user.",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "GET Subjects (1st — cache miss)",
                    "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["console.log('1st GET /subjects responseTime =', pm.response.responseTime, 'ms');"] } }],
